    The correlation matrix in this case is a 2x2 matrix of ones:

    >>> x = jnp.array([[0, 1, 2],
    ...                [0, 1, 2]])
    >>> jnp.corrcoef(x)
    Array([[1., 1.],
           [1., 1.]], dtype=float32)

    Now consider these observations of two variables that are perfectly
    anti-correlated. The correlation matrix in this case has ``-1`` in the
    off-diagonal:

    >>> x = jnp.array([[-1,  0,  1],
    ...                [ 1,  0, -1]])
